NOTE on parity scope: the manifest record for page:vehicles/VehicleDetail extracts exactly two
dataSources (findEffectiveSetting + useVehicleSettings → GET /vehicles/{vehicleId}/settings), one panel
(GlassPanel1), three states (loading/error/success) and 19 strings — requiredCount=23. The generator
captured the page's two NAMED settings hooks (the rest of the web page composes inline
useQuery(request(...)) reads + child components that are their own parity units). The native port binds
that one settings data source, reproduces the web nickname resolver
(findEffectiveSetting(settings,'nickname') → page title) verbatim, lays out the single Mica GlassPanel1
hosting the sixteen <SectionErrorBoundary fallbackTitle=…> regions (the 16 vehicles.detail.section.*Failed
strings ARE those boundary titles), and ports the header wake affordance whose toasts are
vehicles.detail.wakeSuccess / wakeFailed.

## Architecture mapping (web → native)

- useVehicleSettings(id)   → VehicleDetailPageClientFeed (Registration.SettingsOperation =
                            get_api_v1_vehicles_vehicleID_settings, GET /vehicles/{id}/settings) — the
                            primary read; its failure drives the page error state. (ApiEndpoints.cs L545.)
- findEffectiveSetting     → VehicleSettingsData.Find + VehicleDetailProjection nickname resolver
                            (ValueIsText && value != '' ? value : title), ported verbatim from the web
                            typeof value === 'string' guard.
- wake mutation           → VehicleDetailPageClientFeed.WakeAsync (Registration.WakeOperation =
                            post_api_v1_vehicles_vehicleID_wake, POST /vehicles/{id}/wake) →
                            ViewModel.WakeAsync → WakeStatus (wakeSuccess on success, API message else
                            wakeFailed on error), exactly as the web onSuccess/onError handlers.
- isLoading / error       → VehicleDetailPageViewModel.LoadAsync → VehicleDetailState (Loading/Empty/Error/
                            Success) → Display.Show{Loading,Empty,Error,Content}.
- t(...) / useTranslation → ILocalizer.GetString (web key names verbatim) via VehicleDetailStrings.Resolve.
- Units                   : the bound settings values are non-measure (nickname text, booleans, scalar
                            counts), so there is nothing to convert at the display boundary; no non-SI
                            value is stored or computed (P1/S5 honored vacuously for this unit).

