## Summary

Native C#-markup WinUI 3 parity port of the web VehicleDetailPage composition shell, following the
established sibling-page convention (Model/Source/ViewModel/.cs + headless .csproj compile-seam tests).
The bound web data source (useVehicleSettings → GET /vehicles/{id}/settings) is read through the
generated OpenAPI client feed; the nickname resolver (findEffectiveSetting) is ported verbatim and feeds
the page title; the single Mica GlassPanel1 hosts all sixteen SectionErrorBoundary regions, each carrying
its localized fallback title and a never-blank real-data-or-empty body; the header wake affordance posts
the wake command and surfaces wakeSuccess / wakeFailed in a live banner; loading / empty / error / success
states are all implemented; every visible string flows through ILocalizer with web key names preserved
(all 19 required keys + common.wakeUp already present in the resw catalog — 0 added);
AutomationProperties names cover the page, the wake affordance, the banner, the error surface and every
section. Build + lint + test + placeholder gates are green and parity coverage is 23/23 (GlassPanel1 +
loading/error/success + all 19 i18n keys). One pre-existing CA1822 build break in the unrelated
MQTTInspectorPage was fixed (analyzer-prescribed `static`) to reach a green build — documented above. The
only red anywhere in the windows suite is the pre-existing TeslaSync.App.UITests shell suite (absent
WinAppDriver/Appium runner) — an environmental condition this unit neither introduces nor touches.

